  "worked_solution": "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th rows of $A$ are $-3$, $4$, and $2$, respectively.\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $-3+4+2=3.$",
